cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic or scientific research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "TAXIDE: Taxonomic Integrated Development Environment"
abstract: >-
  TAXIDE (Taxonomic Integrated Development Environment) is a 100% pure Haskell
  environment for describing, validating, and computing morphological taxonomic
  matrices. Treating taxonomy as code, TAXIDE formalizes descriptive biology with
  algebraic data types, provides a real-time terminal UI (TUI) with taxonomic linting,
  native in-memory inference engines replacing legacy DELTA/CONFOR/KEY/DIST suites,
  exact cladistic parsimony algorithms (Fitch, Sankoff/Wagner), phenetic distance
  matrices (Gower coefficient), and cross-target compilation to NEXUS, TNT, JSON,
  and high-performance columnar binary formats (HDF5/AVX-512).
